    "A company stores user session records in an Amazon DynamoDB table that uses provisioned capacity. Each session record must be retained for 24 hours after it is created and then removed. Currently, a scheduled job scans the table every hour and deletes expired items, which consumes a large amount of read and write capacity. Which solution will reduce costs the MOST?",
